<p>The U.S.-Israel war with Iran kept widening, with Israel launching what it called a new “broad wave of strikes” in Tehran. U.S. officials said Iran’s air defenses have been “severely degraded” after several days of attacks. Iran also broadened its retaliation across the region, including strikes targeting U.S. bases in the Gulf, heightening fears the fighting could spill further across the Middle East. Energy markets are watching a parallel flashpoint. Iran’s Revolutionary Guards said they have “complete control” of the Strait of Hormuz, the crucial oil-shipping corridor, as oil prices climbed on worries that the conflict—and Iranian pressure on the waterway—could disrupt global fuel trade. Gulf neighbors warned that Iran’s retaliatory fire could pull them into the fighting, adding urgency to efforts to contain escalation even as operations continue.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/VPS58Fs344JY81lw-rV8bBVfn54eSkzMRiFikT2HesWk76hyopW1i6bb9cNjgJ0w35g_nJ1Khqoc29PQT3v23Ql9IMa5N_j3QQeIH9fwWKcWleBORh4dKJnOo5jkF44_V8DNZ2DPcLY4ub4tOLxuNndigerjlU3LFTKlNQ3MBUDrbQrYvrQvumCjMSCqIPt-WeAVEwprDgnabX4dImM' alt='Extinguishing a fire at the site of an airstrike in Beirut, Lebanon, on Wednesday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Troops in Lebanon: CBS said Israel sent troops into Lebanon as the conflict pushed beyond Iran and Israel’s immediate borders.</li><li>Iran’s domestic context: NPR said Iran was preparing for the funeral of Supreme Leader Ali Khamenei even as strikes continued.</li><li>Scale claim: The Straits Times said U.S. officials estimate roughly 2,000 targets have been hit as Iran retaliates across the Gulf.</li><li>No timeline: President Trump defended the war but did not offer a timeline for the campaign, according to CBS’s live updates.</li><li>Threat language: President Trump warned Tehran “is going to be in for a lot of hurt” as the campaign intensified.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Israeli campaign footprint: The Guardian said Israel described its latest strikes as “broad-scale,” hitting targets in both Tehran and Beirut. Kurdish media reported strikes on police stations and IRGC-linked sites in Iran’s north-west. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/04/israel-fresh-strikes-tehran-beirut-iran-targets-us-bases-gulf'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>U.S. military targeting: The Straits Times quoted U.S. military officials saying they are focusing on ballistic missiles and other systems that could threaten U.S. forces. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/topshots-us-says-2000-targets-hit-as-iran-retaliates-across-gulf'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Regional spillover: The New York Times laid out knock-on effects across multiple countries, including reported impacts in places such as Kuwait and Lebanon as the conflict spread beyond Iran and Israel. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/02/world/middleeast/iran-attacks-damage-what-to-know.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>President Trump: NPR’s morning brief said the president argued the U.S. acted because Iran would have struck first. (<a href='https://www.npr.org/2026/03/04/nx-s1-5732274/morning-news-brief'>NPR</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/israel-launches-new-strikes-as-iran-squeezes-key-oil-shipping-route-strait-of-hormuz/article70702385.ece'>Israel launches new strikes as Iran squeezes key oil shipping route Strait of Hormuz</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/02/world/middleeast/iran-attacks-damage-what-to-know.html'>How the Bombing of Iran Is Affecting Lebanon, Kuwait and Other Countries</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/04/israel-fresh-strikes-tehran-beirut-iran-targets-us-bases-gulf'>Israel carries out fresh strikes on Tehran and Beirut as Iran targets US bases in Gulf</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/live-updates/iran-war-us-israel-day-4-trump-